{"agent":"main","body":{"args_hash":"sha256:a1060b45ecb7441027d9aeca42743fa24f9eb9e824517140b887e4115fb64f56","args_inline":{"content":"---\nname: selectfordeletion-contract-frozen\ndescription: snapkeep's selectForDeletion has a frozen contract - positional callers, newest-first string ids, pinned = legal hold\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`selectForDeletion(backups, policy)` in `src/prune.ts` is consumed by the scheduler plus two other services that call it positionally, so the signature cannot change. The scheduler deletes every id it returns with no undo, and diffs the returned ids against the previous run to alert on anything unexpected — so the return shape stays a newest-first list of string ids. Snapshots tagged `pinned` are legal holds (list from legal went live 2026-09-14) and must never appear in the result; all other tags (`replicated`, `verified`, …) are free-form and carry no retention meaning.\n\n**Why:** Two earlier fixes to this file each corrected one rule and broke another; the callers and the no-undo delete make changes here unusually costly.\n\n**How to apply:** When touching `src/prune.ts`, keep edits minimal and local to the rule in question, leave `isoWeek`, the daily rule, and the sort order alone (their tests live in the scheduler repo), and treat `test/prune.test.ts`'s existing case as the acceptance test rather than something to adjust.\n","file_path":"/var/folders/yb/b_617z_s2ml933nmr_k7m47m0000gn/T/saga-bench-3578220652/ts-0011-backup-prune-amnesia/2/cfg/claude-config/projects/-private-var-folders-yb-b-617z-s2ml933nmr-k7m47m0000gn-T-saga-bench-3578220652-ts-0011-backup-prune-amnesia-2-ws/memory/selectfordeletion-contract-frozen.md"},"component":"harness","cwd_rel":".","index_version":null,"tool":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01PrCHSSVAEwsRBSqWUFn9AL"},"hash":"sha256:77ec15f9464fed331c35b48bd21959e71e45b1a7e2c396ae7604e38ca99e900c","mono_ns":21000000,"prev":"sha256:87ce6ea77089ee1d24f379971495a016f1c783f3256f6b7879da323f56f65c52","s